Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From c59e02f29b81d2070da8f5d4e9955e52d959623a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:06:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3582/3586] drm/rockchip: vop2: Add support for RK3528

The RK3528 VOP is a hybrid of the rk3568/rk3588 and rk3576 VOPs:
- the interface mux, polarity and interrupt registers are the same as
  on rk3568 (one shared irq, HDMI0 output only on VP0),
- the overlay is done per video port like on rk3576 (OVL_CTRL,
  LAYER_SEL, MIX, HDR and BG mixer registers at 0x600 + vp * 0x100),
- the window to VP mapping is done with a shared OVL_SYS_PORT_SEL
  register (0x504), the window delay registers live in the OVL_SYS block.

It has two video ports:
- VP0: up to 4096x2304@60, connected to the HDMI TX,
- VP1: up to 720x576, only connected to the TV encoder,
and one Cluster window plus four Esmart windows.

The Esmart line buffers are configured in the 4K + 2K + 2K mode (as in
the vendor kernel), which leaves Esmart1 unusable and limits the output
width of Esmart2/3 to 2048 pixels. Add an optional per window output size
limit to enforce the latter in atomic_check.

Also take care of some rk3528 specifics found in the vendor kernel:
- the aclk pre auto gating must be disabled,
- the vertical pre-scale down must be triggered earlier for sources wider
  than 1920 pixels, as the VOP processes 2 pixels per cycle,
- YUV444 output needs the RG swap like rk3576/rk3588,
- the build number of the VERSION_INFO register differs between chip
  revisions (0x50171263 in the vendor kernel, 0x50174334 seen on a
  RK3528A), so only check the major/minor version.

Gamma LUT, HDR, ACM and post-CSC are not supported yet.

Based on the Rockchip vendor kernel (develop-6.1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
